  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SIDA Integrated humanitarian mine action to support early recovery in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is &quot;Addressing the humanitarian impact of mines/ explosive ordnance on conflict-affected communities in Ukraine and enable early economic recovery.&quot; The project is implemented by Danish Refugee Council (DRC) during the period 1 September 2023 to 31 December 2026 and is a continuation of previous Sida support under the Sustainable Peace strategy since 2018.DRC&apos;s mine action operations in Ukraine includes most components of mine action including: non-technical survey, mine clearance/land release, Explosive Ordnance Risk Education, Victim Assistance, training and equipment for government entities as well as Improved participation of women in mine action in Ukraine. Due to the last goal and integration in the project design the project is marked as 1 on the gender marker.</narrative>
  </description>
